    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e45d56f9",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes the 9/11 terrorist attacks with a photo of a Muslim woman in Congress in 2019, implying that Muslims are responsible for or should be blamed for the 9/11 attacks. This is a direct attack on Muslims based on their religion, invoking the harmful stereotype of associating Islam with terrorism. The text 'defund homeland security!' further reinforces the hateful intent by suggesting that Muslims are responsible for the need for homeland security, which is a dangerous and false equivalence. The meme uses the traumatic event of 9/11 to stigmatize and demonize Muslims, which is a clear example of Islamophobia and hateful content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_54df4c61"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
